          "source_block": 4,
          "candidate_block": 4,
          "candidate_line_count": 6,
          "center_error": 13.203,
          "text": "Article 1 In accordance with the guiding opinions on high­quality business operations of\nthe joint­stock company, and in conjunction with the relevant requirements of the Group\nCompany's Implementation Rules for High­Quality Business Operations (Trial) (CCECC\nOperations [2024] No. 341), these Measures are specially formulated to\ncomprehensively improve project operation quality, effectively manage the company's\ndomestic business operations, and standardize business procedures and workflows."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 8,
          "candidate_block": 5,
          "candidate_line_count": 3,
          "center_error": 14.914,
          "text": "Article 2 Projects in these Measures refer to various types of the Company's\nbusiness operations undertaken through direct entrustment or bidding, such as\nconsulting, survey, design, supervision, and engineering general contracting."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 10,
          "candidate_block": 6,
          "candidate_line_count": 4,
          "center_error": 15.291,
          "text": "Article 3 In principle, business undertaking work shall follow the procedure of first project assessment, then\napplication for approval, and finally contract signing. Article 4 When carrying out project business undertaking\nwork, factors such as the Company's development strategy, business direction, responsibility cost, production\nand technical capabilities, and current status"
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 12,
          "candidate_block": 7,
          "candidate_line_count": 6,
          "center_error": 13.315,
          "text": "Article 4 shall be comprehensively considered. In accordance with the\nprocedural provisions of these Measures, the work of such stages as\n\"information tracking, project assessment and application, bid document\npreparation and review, contract negotiation, contract review and signing,\nowner services during project implementation, and project return visits\" shall be\ncompleted."
        },
        {
